{"seq":6,"at":"2026-10-21","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a2628"},"reason":"Proofread (reasons in the entries above / the batch report).","by":"enrich batch 224","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-enrich/enrich-report/a1824-a0468.md","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",358],["-","2006;"],["+","2006."],["=",1],["+","The standard fixes only "],["=",2],["-","cylinder's"],["+","shoulder:"],["=",1],["-","body"],["+","industrial"],["=",1],["-","may"],["+","cylinders"],["=",1],["-","be"],["+","usually"],["=",1],["-","any"],["+","have"],["=",1],["-","colour"],["+","a"],["=",1],["+","grey body or one matching "],["=",2],["-","supplier"],["+","shoulder,"],["=",1],["-","likes."],["+","white"],["=",1],["+","bodies are kept for medical gases, and bottled LPG such as propane and butane is not covered at all. "],["=",152],["+","So the shoulder of an oxygen cylinder is white, that of a nitrogen cylinder black and that of an argon cylinder dark green.\n\n"],["=",42],["+","bottles "],["=",123]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",304],["-","2006;"],["+","2006."],["=",1],["-","der"],["+","Die"],["=",1],["-","Flaschenmantel"],["+","Norm"],["=",1],["-","darf"],["+","legt"],["=",1],["-","jede"],["+","nur"],["=",1],["-","beliebige"],["+","die"],["=",1],["-","Farbe"],["+","Schulter"],["=",1],["-","des"],["+","fest:"],["=",1],["-","Lieferanten"],["+","Industriegasflaschen"],["=",1],["-","tragen."],["+","haben"],["=",1],["+","meist einen grauen oder schulterfarbenen Mantel, weiße Mäntel sind den medizinischen Gasen vorbehalten, und Flüssiggasflaschen wie Propan und Butan fallen gar nicht darunter. "],["=",140],["+","Bei einer Sauerstoffflasche ist die Schulter also weiß, bei einer Stickstoffflasche schwarz und bei einer Argonflasche dunkelgrün.\n\n"],["=",135]]}],"hash":"cb1637d8961d"},
